                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parasynonym",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e283ccca-4697-3b8f-8602-28b56b97f468",
                                        "entry_id": "21d7054a-b82d-35ba-b0bd-b716869b2b9b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A term (word or phrase) which is parasynonymous with others, but not necessarily considered a synonym."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eead5b5d-597e-40e5-98db-dc6b0bc7e31a",
                                                "sense_id": "e283ccca-4697-3b8f-8602-28b56b97f468",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: synonym"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "316bb358-7d39-4fc1-8ea8-b7a72317ee03",
                        "source_entry_id": "2f8f7696-56ce-322d-b647-93f02f1fcda6",
                        "source_sense_id": "f8ad9749-f264-3df4-a5bf-1f961d9555dd",
                        "target_lang_word": "plesionym",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plesionym",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e9effa0-49db-3bf9-a749-664742365c8c",
                                        "entry_id": "ccfeb07d-2c89-3289-b97b-d5d17f8a322b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of parasynonym."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4027f9b9-ba5a-4914-ad42-a0e0ec0c4120",
                                                "sense_id": "5e9effa0-49db-3bf9-a749-664742365c8c",
                                                "text": "It was suggested in 12.1 that propositional synonyms are 'more synonymous' than plesionyms, which, in turn, are 'more synonymous' than non-synonyms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76e9a102-1da9-414e-9948-dd8e241590cb",
                                                "sense_id": "5e9effa0-49db-3bf9-a749-664742365c8c",
                                                "text": "An immediate question is when does a plesionym cross a \"vertical distance boundary\" to become a different concept?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47966515-b273-4618-afed-17f8a31a1042",
                                                "sense_id": "5e9effa0-49db-3bf9-a749-664742365c8c",
                                                "text": "Such a semantic intertextual frame arises when the lexical item 'mist' is linked to its plesionym 'fog' and an intertextual link between two texts containing these lexical items is created."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aed68139-5fe9-4fdd-8286-68b3fd0b5f6b",
                                                "sense_id": "5e9effa0-49db-3bf9-a749-664742365c8c",
                                                "text": "A word is a plesionym if it is a near-synonym, but substitution of the word does not leave the same truth conditions. For example, it 'It wasn't misty, just foggy', the words 'misty' and 'foggy' are pleisonyms of each other. […] Plesionyms are often used to indicate that the speaker is grappling after precision, but perhaps does not possess the precise vocabulary or technical term for the object in mind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
